                            beginner: [
                                {
                                    content: `<h3>What is HTML5?</h3>
• HTML5 is the current version of HTML, and the one you will always use.<br>
• It made web pages able to do things that previously needed Flash plugins.<br><br>

<h3>Main Additions</h3>
• <b>Semantic tags</b> - header, nav, main, section, article, aside, footer.<br>
• <b>Media tags</b> - audio and video play natively, no plugin needed.<br>
• <b>Graphics</b> - canvas and inline SVG.<br>
• <b>New form inputs</b> - email, date, number, color, range.<br>
• <b>Built-in validation</b> - required and pattern work without JavaScript.<br>
• <b>Storage APIs</b> - localStorage and sessionStorage.<br>
• <b>Simplified DOCTYPE</b> and charset declaration.`,
                                    codeExamples: [
                                        `<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>HTML5 Features Demo</title>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Semantic structure -->
  <header>
    <h1>JavaSchoolLab</h1>
    <nav><a href="#courses">Courses</a></nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <article>
      <h2>Learning HTML5</h2>
      <p>Semantic tags describe meaning, not appearance.</p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <!-- Native media, no plugin -->
  <video controls width="320">
    <source src="lesson.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    Your browser does not support video.
  </video>

  <!-- Modern form input with built-in validation -->
  <form>
    <input type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
    <input type="date">
    <button type="submit">Send</button>
  </form>

  <footer><p>&copy; 2025</p></footer>

</body>
</html>`,
                                    ]
                                }
                            ],
                            intermediate: [
                                {
                                    content: `<h3>HTML5 vs HTML4 - Quick Comparison</h3>
• <b>DOCTYPE</b> - HTML4 needed a long DTD line, HTML5 needs one short line.<br>
• <b>Charset</b> - HTML4 used a long meta http-equiv, HTML5 uses meta charset.<br>
• <b>Structure</b> - HTML4 used div id="header", HTML5 uses &lt;header&gt;.<br>
• <b>Media</b> - HTML4 needed Flash, HTML5 has audio and video.<br>
• <b>Validation</b> - HTML4 needed JavaScript, HTML5 has required and pattern.<br>
• <b>Storage</b> - HTML4 had cookies only, HTML5 adds localStorage.<br><br>

<h3>Why Semantic Tags Beat Divs</h3>
• A page full of divs tells the browser nothing about meaning.<br>
• Screen readers use semantic tags to offer landmark navigation.<br>
• Search engines use them to understand which part is the real content.<br>
• Other developers read the structure instantly.`,
                                    codeExamples: [
                                        `<!-- HTML4 thinking: divs with id names -->
<div id="header">...</div>
<div id="nav">...</div>
<div id="main">...</div>
<div id="footer">...</div>


<!-- HTML5 thinking: the tag itself carries the meaning -->
<header>...</header>
<nav>...</nav>
<main>...</main>
<footer>...</footer>`,
                                    ]
                                }
                            ],
                            expert: [
                                {
                                    content: `<h3>Feature Detection, Not Browser Detection</h3>
• Never check <i>which browser</i> is running - check <i>whether the feature exists</i>.<br>
• Browser sniffing breaks the moment a new version or browser appears.<br>
• Feature detection keeps working forever.<br><br>

<h3>Progressive Enhancement</h3>
• Build a page that works with plain HTML first.<br>
• Then add HTML5 and JavaScript features on top for browsers that support them.<br>
• Users on old or limited devices still get a working page instead of a blank one.<br>
• This is why &lt;video&gt; allows fallback content between its tags.`,
                                    codeExamples: [
                                        `<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Feature Detection</title></head>
<body>

<p id="result"></p>

<script>
  // WRONG - browser sniffing, breaks constantly
  // if (navigator.userAgent.indexOf("Chrome") > -1) { ... }

  // RIGHT - ask whether the feature exists
  var messages = [];

  if ("localStorage" in window) {
    messages.push("localStorage supported");
  }

  // Does this browser understand input type=date?
  var probe = document.createElement("input");
  probe.setAttribute("type", "date");
  if (probe.type === "date") {
    messages.push("date input supported");
  } else {
    messages.push("date input NOT supported, showing text box instead");
  }

  document.getElementById("result").textContent = messages.join(" | ");
</script>

</body>
</html>`,
                                    ]
                                }
                            ],
