                                    content: `<h3>4. Syntax and Parts of an Absolute URL</h3>
• Full form: <b>protocol://subdomain.domain.tld:port/path?query#fragment</b><br><br>

<h3>The Parts Explained</h3>
• <b>protocol</b> - https:// or http://. Always use https.<br>
• <b>subdomain</b> - www, blog, shop. Optional.<br>
• <b>domain</b> - javaschoollab.<br>
• <b>tld</b> - .com, .in, .org.<br>
• <b>port</b> - :8080. Optional, defaults to 443 for https.<br>
• <b>path</b> - /courses/java.html.<br>
• <b>query</b> - ?level=basic&amp;sort=new. Extra data.<br>
• <b>fragment</b> - #section2. Jumps to a part of the page.`,
