                                    content: `<h3>8. Interview Questions</h3>
• <b>Q: What is the difference between an absolute and a relative URL?</b><br>
A: An absolute URL contains the scheme and host and resolves with no context. A relative URL is resolved against the current document's base URL.<br><br>

• <b>Q: Is /about an absolute URL?</b><br>
A: No. It is <b>root-relative</b>. It still needs the current origin to resolve. Only a URL with a scheme is absolute.<br><br>

• <b>Q: What is an origin?</b><br>
A: Scheme plus host plus port. It determines the same-origin policy, cookies, storage and CORS.<br><br>

• <b>Q: Are http://site.com and https://site.com the same origin?</b><br>
A: No. Different schemes mean different origins, so they do not share cookies or localStorage.<br><br>

• <b>Q: What is an open redirect and how do you prevent it?</b><br>
A: Redirecting to a user-supplied URL. Prevent it by allowing only same-origin paths, never a full URL from input.<br><br>

• <b>Q: encodeURI or encodeURIComponent?</b><br>
A: encodeURIComponent for a single value, encodeURI for a whole URL. Best of all, use the URL API.`,
