                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
• A <b>relative URL</b> gives the address <b>relative to the current page</b>.<br>
• It has no protocol and no domain name.<br>
• Example: about.html, images/logo.png, ../index.html<br><br>

<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic</h3>
• To link between pages <b>within your own website</b>.<br>
• To keep links short and easy to maintain.<br><br>

<h3>3. Need of This Topic</h3>
• Writing the full domain on every internal link is repetitive and fragile.<br>
• If the domain changes, every absolute link must be edited; relative links keep working.<br>
• The same code then runs on localhost, staging and production with no change.`,
