                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
• An <b>internal link</b> is a link that points to another page <b>inside the same website</b>.<br>
• It is written with the &lt;a&gt; tag and a <b>relative URL</b>, for example about.html or /courses/java.html<br>
• The visitor never leaves your domain when the link is clicked.<br><br>

<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic</h3>
• To move the student from one page of the site to another, like Home to Courses to Contact.<br>
• To build the <b>navigation menu</b> that every website needs.<br>
• To connect related content so a reader can keep exploring.<br><br>

<h3>3. Need of This Topic</h3>
• A website is not one page. Without internal links each page is an island.<br>
• Typing the full domain on every link is repetitive and breaks when the domain changes.<br>
• Search engines like Google follow internal links to discover and rank your pages.`,
