                                    content: `<h3>4. Advantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Irregular shapes.</b> Polygons can follow a state border or a machine part outline.<br>
&bull; <b>One image, many links.</b> Only one file is downloaded for the whole map.<br>
&bull; <b>No JavaScript needed.</b> The browser handles all the clicking.<br>
&bull; <b>Keyboard usable.</b> Each area is focusable and works with the Tab key.<br>
<h3>5. Disadvantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Not responsive.</b> Coords are fixed pixel values, so they break when the image is resized on a phone.<br>
&bull; <b>Hard to maintain.</b> If the artwork changes even slightly, every coordinate must be measured again.<br>
&bull; <b>Poor on touch screens.</b> Small areas are difficult to tap accurately.<br>
&bull; <b>Accessibility work.</b> Every area needs its own alt text, and many developers forget it.<br>
&bull; <b>Mostly replaced.</b> Today the same result is usually built with inline svg, which scales properly.<br>`,
