                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition (Advanced)</h3>
&bull; The action is resolved against the document base URL, so a &lt;base&gt; tag or a trailing slash difference changes the final target.<br>
&bull; An empty action="" is legal and means the current URL including its query string, which is a classic source of duplicated query parameters.<br>
&bull; formaction on a submit button, and formmethod, formenctype, formtarget and formnovalidate, override the form level attributes for that one button.<br>
<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic (Advanced)</h3>
&bull; To route one form to several server operations without duplicating markup.<br>
&bull; To keep endpoints stable and versioned, for example /api/v2/orders, so old bookmarks and mobile clients keep working.<br>
<h3>3. Need of This Topic (Advanced)</h3>
&bull; <b>Open redirect and CSRF.</b> Never build an action URL from a query parameter supplied by the user.<br>
&bull; Cross origin posts do not carry SameSite cookies by default, so a payment gateway integration must use a signed token instead of the session.<br>
&bull; A Content Security Policy form-action directive can restrict where any form on the page is allowed to post, which blocks injected forms.`,
